// Feature catalogues for tools/parity.mjs: what the original sites of each Verse page offer, studied from the live sites and their
// documentation (owner, 2026-10-28: be sure ours are actually better, in every way). One row per feature:
//   [id, area, what the original offers, liveRe, verseRe, partialRe, scope]
//   liveRe    words that show the feature on an original site's own pages (a match is the evidence that this site has it)
//   verseRe   words in the Verse page's own source that show Verse has it (the match, with file and line, is the evidence)
//   partialRe weaker words: Verse has part of it
//   scope     'core' = every original site of this page has it; an array = the named sites have it (studied by hand); empty = only the sites
//             whose pages show it (liveRe)
// Sites are named in plain text only. A row whose Verse status is wrong is fixed here, never in the generated docs.
const T = (s) => new RegExp(s, 'i'); // every pattern is a constant string in this file, never input (void-review: ok)
